>   Using "pare" as the argument to "ju'u" is asking for trouble.

Non-sense! This is perfectly valid Lojban. It just means the part before
=93ju'u=94 is in base 12. The base=92s base is 10 by default. You can also
override that by appending ju'u to the base. You can theoreticall add
as many =93ju'u=94s as you wish but the last base must be in base 10.

Read the reference grammar.
<http://dag.github.io/cll/18/10/>

